<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Copyright 2026 Zachary Olkin. All rights reserved.

Cyclone DDS interface pinning for the ZED depth box.

Copy to `cyclonedds.xml` in this directory, set the address to THIS box's robot network
address, and point the container at it from docker/.env:

    CYCLONEDDS_URI=file:///opt/zed_config/cyclonedds.xml

then recreate the container: compose reads .env only when it CREATES one, so the force
recreate flag is required. The path is the one INSIDE the container; this directory is bind mounted there
read only, which is why the file lives beside the node params rather than next to .env.

NO DOUBLE HYPHEN ANYWHERE IN A COMMENT IN THIS FILE. A double hyphen is illegal inside an
XML comment and conforming parsers reject the whole file, even though Cyclone's own parser
tolerates it. The obelisk example carries the same warning for the same reason.

WHY THIS BOX NEEDS ONE AT ALL
=============================
Not for the usual reason. Discovery here is plain multicast on a wired switch and works
without any of this. The problem is that the box is MULTI HOMED: wifi for internet, the
robot network for DDS, plus the l4tbr0 and docker0 bridges. Cyclone picks ONE interface and
says so in its own log:

    using network interface enP8p1s0 (udp/192.168.123.221) selected arbitrarily from:
        enP8p1s0, wlP7p1s0, l4tbr0, docker0

"Selected arbitrarily" is the whole issue. All four rank equally, so the choice can land on
wifi or on a docker bridge, and then the brain never sees a depth frame while this box looks
perfectly healthy and the node logs nothing wrong. That is the silent failure
`scripts/net_check.sh` exists to name.

An ADDRESS rather than an interface name: a driver assigned name changes when the adapter
does, and the address is the thing that was chosen deliberately.

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
=============================
* AllowMulticast is left at its default (on). The unicast Peers list in the obelisk example
  exists for links that will not carry multicast, such as wifi or a routed hop. A wired
  switch carries it, and turning multicast off would then oblige every box to list every
  other one, which is a maintenance burden and an asymmetry bug waiting to happen.
* SocketReceiveBufferSize is not set. The obelisk boxes ask for 10 MB because they RECEIVE
  the 500 Hz encoder and 1 kHz IMU streams. This box receives nothing and publishes two
  30x26 float images at about 45 Hz, so the default is ample. That also keeps the file from
  being fatal on a stock kernel: a buffer request the kernel cannot satisfy kills every ROS
  node at startup with "rmw_create_node: failed to create domain", and this box ships with
  net.core.rmem_max at 1 MB. Raising it to 16 MB is still worth doing for fleet consistency,
  but nothing here depends on it.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface address="192.168.123.221" priority="default" multicast="default" />
      </Interfaces>
    </General>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
